<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE JUNE BANK CREDIT RISES 11.4 PCT ON YEAR.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE JUNE BANK CREDIT RISES 11.4 PCT ON YEAR.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank credit to non-bank customers (in billions of Singapore dollars):</p>
<p>						 June 97  May 97   June 96</p>
<p>Total (including financial bills)    132.97   131.90   119.36</p>
<p>Agriculture, mining, quarrying	   0.178    0.159    0.162</p>
<p>Manufacturing				 12.35    12.65    11.78</p>
<p>Building, construction		    44.06    44.18    38.67</p>
<p>General commerce			    24.98    24.46    22.79</p>
<p>Transport, storage, communication	3.19     3.07     2.44</p>
<p>Financial institutions		    19.38    19.05    18.22</p>
<p>Personal loans				22.01    21.66    18.99</p>
<p>Others					   6.81     6.68     6.31</p>
<p>The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said bank credit moderated in June, growing at a slower rate of 11.4 percent, compared with 12.6 percent in May. Overall credit growth was dampened by a slowdown in loans mostly to the building and construction, and manufacturing sectors.</p>
